        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under purified N2, Ho metal filings (0.50 g, 3.03 mmol), HOQ (0.30 g, 2.07 mmol), strontium metal (0.53 g, 6.06 mmol), tBuB (0.30 g) and Hg (4 drops) were placed in a Carius tube, evacuated, sealed and heated to 190 °C for 3 d, giving a mixture of red glass (predominant) and yellow crystals. The tBuB was removed by sublimation and the small yellow crystals of 1 were isolated by hand picking (yield ~10%). An alternative preactivation route also gave 1: Ho metal (0.86 g, 5.21 mmol), Sr (0.3 g, 3.75 mmol) and 7 drops of Hg were heated in an evacuated sealed Carius tube at 350 °C for 2 d, then reopened under N2, charged with HOQ (0.50 g, 3.44 mmol) and tBuB (0.25 g, 1.02 mmol), resealed under vacuum and reheated at 190 °C for 2 d (yield ~5%). Control reactions of Ho or Sr alone with HOQ under analogous conditions gave only red glassy solids.",
